    "summary": "# Briefing\n\n## Finding\n**No RFP in the provided corpus expressly contains an Iran-related certification, disclosure, or compliance requirement for respondents.**\n\n## Closest Potentially Relevant RFP\n### Texas Municipal Retirement System (TMRS) – Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services  \n**Issued:** February 3, 2022\n\n- The draft agreement includes respondent/contractor representations that:\n  - **Section 5.1.6:** the consultant **does not boycott Israel** and will not do so during the contract term.\n  - **Section 5.1.7:** the consultant **does not boycott energy companies** and will not do so during the contract term.\n- These are **explicit compliance representations**, but they are **not Iran-specific**.\n\n## RFPs Reviewed With No Iran-Related Respondent Requirements Found\n- **OCERS Investment Consultant Services RFP (2021)**\n- **Kern County Employees’ Retirement Association Actuarial Audit Services RFP (2024)**\n- **SURS Emerging Markets Equity RFP (2022 sample)**\n- **Apple Valley Fire Protection District OPEB Actuarial Services RFP (2024)**\n- **Cook County Fund Manager of Managers RFP (2025)**\n- **OCERS Pension Administration System Consulting RFP (2023)**\n- **Arizona PSPRS Non-Discretionary Investment Consultant Services RFP (2021)**\n\n## Conclusion\nBased on the supplied evidence, **none of the RFPs contain an Iran-related certification, disclosure, or compliance requirement**. The **TMRS RFP** is the only item with a related geopolitical compliance representation, but it concerns **Israel boycott** and **energy company boycott** provisions, **not Iran**."
